WEBVTT

00:22.022 --> 00:26.943
TRAGEDY ON THE WAVES

00:27.736 --> 00:33.908
If you keep spilling so much blood,
our customers will stop coming!

00:35.827 --> 00:38.705
The melon leaves...

00:39.205 --> 00:42.000
have grown in number.

00:44.294 --> 00:45.962
<i>He's speaking to Melon.</i>

00:46.046 --> 00:49.674
I'm not carrying any more
dead bodies out of here.

00:50.341 --> 00:52.010
So? What'll it be?

00:54.471 --> 00:55.555
I'm still thinking...

00:56.264 --> 00:58.558
I recommend the black bunny.

01:00.226 --> 01:05.023
<i>This must be the strange pattern
Cosmo was talking about.</i>

01:05.106 --> 01:08.651
They look better...

01:08.735 --> 01:11.905
than leopard spots.

01:13.490 --> 01:15.492
Are you scared?

01:16.618 --> 01:22.499
<i>Could Melon's body be changing
like my mother's did?</i>

01:23.625 --> 01:26.336
Are you... worried?

01:28.171 --> 01:31.049
You must be... lonely.

01:33.259 --> 01:35.136
You're...

01:35.678 --> 01:39.224
always... alone.

01:40.141 --> 01:41.267
<i>Of course.</i>

01:42.310 --> 01:45.063
<i>Here I am thinking he's a bad guy,</i>

01:45.688 --> 01:47.857
<i>but in reality he's just another beast.</i>

01:48.566 --> 01:52.195
If only... there was...

01:52.278 --> 01:57.408
someone... who understood you...

01:58.159 --> 01:59.244
Have you decided?

02:01.996 --> 02:04.833
Is... that... so?

02:05.625 --> 02:11.131
Going to see... the Reaper's Blooddrop...?

02:12.549 --> 02:14.759
The Reaper's Blooddrop?

02:15.844 --> 02:19.264
May... your heart...

02:19.347 --> 02:25.979
find... inner... peace...

02:37.448 --> 02:40.535
ANTI-CRIME CAMPAIGN
LET'S LIVE TOGETHER

02:40.618 --> 02:41.870
Okay.

02:42.537 --> 02:43.454
Tape please.

02:49.127 --> 02:52.422
I'm here to see
the Beastar on urgent business.

02:52.922 --> 02:55.717
Excuse me? There is no Beastar--

02:55.800 --> 02:58.595
I was told to meet him
on the top floor of the police station.

02:58.678 --> 02:59.512
That's...

02:59.596 --> 03:02.807
Don't tell me you believed
such a wild rumor!

03:04.475 --> 03:06.019
Yes, I'm only kidding.

03:08.271 --> 03:10.773
I was summoned
by the Crime Prevention Bureau.

03:11.274 --> 03:12.942
Identification, please.

03:13.985 --> 03:15.445
Is my student ID okay?

03:15.528 --> 03:16.529
Sure.

03:18.448 --> 03:21.159
A popular idol is coming today.

03:22.327 --> 03:24.996
They have to appeal
to the kids, after all.

03:25.622 --> 03:26.497
Here.

03:26.998 --> 03:29.626
Take elevator E to the 38th floor.

03:29.709 --> 03:31.044
Thank you.

03:34.547 --> 03:37.759
Pardon me, but how many floors
does this building have?

03:37.842 --> 03:39.344
One hundred and eight.

03:39.427 --> 03:41.846
Too many to take the stairs, huh?

03:41.930 --> 03:44.641
Who would do such a thing?

03:46.476 --> 03:47.477
You're right.

03:57.946 --> 04:00.031
<i>If I can just persuade the Beastar...</i>

04:03.868 --> 04:05.495
<i>Only 55 more floors.</i>

04:06.955 --> 04:08.831
<i>Will I make it on this leg?</i>

04:17.006 --> 04:18.007
Five.

04:18.091 --> 04:19.425
I'm out!

04:19.509 --> 04:20.969
You didn't say the word.

04:21.886 --> 04:23.346
Last place again!

04:23.429 --> 04:25.974
Damn it, I was winning, too!

04:29.352 --> 04:31.354
<i>Why do the stairs end here?</i>

04:42.782 --> 04:44.826
<i>Thank you, Shishi-Gumi.</i>

04:59.841 --> 05:01.801
It's the emergency staircase
on the 100th floor.

05:03.094 --> 05:04.971
I'll go check.

05:05.054 --> 05:06.806
- The game can wait.
- Hey, wait.

05:06.889 --> 05:08.016
Hey!

05:13.313 --> 05:14.647
<i>That leads up.</i>

05:38.671 --> 05:40.631
100th floor hallway clear.

05:41.382 --> 05:42.967
<i>Another malfunction?</i>

05:43.885 --> 05:45.011
I'll check.

06:04.572 --> 06:05.573
Hey!

06:06.491 --> 06:07.492
Wait!

06:11.954 --> 06:13.498
Open up! Hey!

06:16.292 --> 06:17.668
Hey!

06:37.313 --> 06:39.524
Come on out, little deer.

06:40.483 --> 06:41.943
Damn it!

06:43.027 --> 06:44.403
Where'd you go?

06:58.251 --> 07:01.587
<i>We've got an intruder!
A young deer! Find him!</i>

07:09.262 --> 07:11.139
"Combined drama club"?

07:11.222 --> 07:15.309
Please allow the carnivores
and herbivores to work together.

07:15.393 --> 07:17.812
We want to participate
in the festival together.

07:18.438 --> 07:20.565
I can't allow that.

07:20.648 --> 07:23.484
You should know that better than anyone.

07:23.568 --> 07:25.027
Of course we do.

07:25.111 --> 07:28.823
There were a few unfortunate incidents
in the drama club last year.

07:29.657 --> 07:31.492
That's exactly why we want to do this!

07:31.576 --> 07:33.786
FESTIVAL OF THE METEOR
REAPPLICATION FORM

07:33.870 --> 07:38.291
There's something we need to do.
Carnivores and herbivores together!

07:38.875 --> 07:40.126
That's why?

07:40.209 --> 07:41.210
Yes.

07:42.962 --> 07:45.548
And the program will be <i>Adler the Reaper...</i>

07:46.132 --> 07:47.175
Yes.

07:47.258 --> 07:48.259
Why?

07:48.342 --> 07:52.889
It's a story about sacrificing one's life
out of love for another species.

07:52.972 --> 07:55.766
This work is special to the drama club.

07:55.850 --> 07:58.978
We haven't decided who'll play Adler,

07:59.061 --> 08:01.689
- but we're getting ther--
- Hold on, now.

08:02.315 --> 08:04.859
That's the message you want to send?

08:05.485 --> 08:08.112
Giving up your life for love?

08:11.324 --> 08:14.994
You should understand,
having experienced a devouring incident.

08:15.578 --> 08:17.872
Death doesn't solve anything.

08:17.955 --> 08:21.626
<i>But...</i> the drama club always performs <i>Adler...</i>

08:21.709 --> 08:23.211
It doesn't matter.

08:24.378 --> 08:28.216
Segregation allows you all
to have a safer school life.

08:28.299 --> 08:29.467
Isn't that right?

08:29.550 --> 08:32.303
Yes. You're right, but...

08:33.513 --> 08:35.556
Do you hope to die like Adler?

08:37.058 --> 08:39.852
I don't want to die...

08:43.064 --> 08:47.235
And yet you still wish to work together?

08:47.818 --> 08:48.986
- Yes.
- Yes.

08:49.987 --> 08:50.821
In that case,

08:51.906 --> 08:54.033
why not put those feelings into a script?

08:54.992 --> 08:55.826
- What?
- What?

08:56.452 --> 09:01.916
I've been thinking we need
a new play to represent the drama club.

09:03.626 --> 09:04.752
- Yes!
- All right!

09:04.835 --> 09:05.878
We'll give it a try.

09:10.508 --> 09:14.554
"Kines is a drug"? I doubt it.

09:14.637 --> 09:16.764
I was just drinking one.

09:18.015 --> 09:19.559
And I feel great!

09:23.396 --> 09:24.438
<i>This is...</i>

09:26.023 --> 09:27.984
What the hell?

09:29.610 --> 09:32.572
<i>He's reacting to the Kines.
This isn't good.</i>

09:46.919 --> 09:48.170
<i>Damn it.</i>

10:06.564 --> 10:10.568
A cop trying to eat an herbivore?
You've got some serious guts.

10:14.113 --> 10:15.114
Are you all right?

10:18.409 --> 10:20.369
So, you're the Beastar?

10:23.873 --> 10:25.041
Thank you.

10:29.920 --> 10:32.048
"KINES IS A DRUG"
THE KINES REPORT

10:32.882 --> 10:34.300
Is this yours?

10:35.343 --> 10:36.177
Yes.

10:36.844 --> 10:38.971
Kines is a dangerous drink.

10:39.680 --> 10:42.767
It appears this guard drank some.

10:43.392 --> 10:47.355
If we don't stop it from being sold,
the same thing will happen elsewhere.

10:48.356 --> 10:51.817
And you played spy
to sneak in here and tell me that?

10:51.901 --> 10:54.028
It won't do you any good to save me alone.

10:57.156 --> 10:59.033
You can do it yourself.

10:59.116 --> 11:00.660
You're a Beastar.

11:00.743 --> 11:03.454
You could solve this problem at the root.

11:04.205 --> 11:05.039
Please.

11:12.046 --> 11:14.965
Okay, let's move on to the photo session.

11:15.049 --> 11:17.259
We'll start with the center shot.

11:17.885 --> 11:18.719
Okay.

11:19.345 --> 11:21.680
Let's... live together!

11:26.268 --> 11:27.686
All right, did we get that?

11:27.770 --> 11:29.313
Next, we'll shoot from the left.

11:37.196 --> 11:38.197
Calm down!

11:39.073 --> 11:41.409
- Stop! What happened to you?
- That's your cue.

11:42.284 --> 11:43.619
Right.

11:46.205 --> 11:47.081
It was Kines!

11:48.624 --> 11:50.459
He drank Kines.

11:51.127 --> 11:52.920
It drove him mad.

11:53.587 --> 11:58.926
Drinking Kines turned him into a beast
with a craving for raw meat!

11:59.009 --> 12:01.178
That's the heir to the Horns Conglomerate!

12:01.262 --> 12:05.057
If I hadn't gotten lucky,
he would've eaten me in the elevator.

12:05.808 --> 12:07.309
At this very moment,

12:07.393 --> 12:09.603
I'd be getting picked apart bit by bit.

12:10.938 --> 12:14.733
<i>Kines is responsible
for multiple devouring incidents.</i>

12:15.526 --> 12:20.531
<i>Even so, it remains on the market
and is being consumed by the masses.</i>

12:21.115 --> 12:22.700
- Look at him go.
<i>- But no longer.</i>

12:22.783 --> 12:26.078
- He's made for the spotlight.
<i>- We must end this.</i>

12:26.579 --> 12:29.331
<i>Everyone, Kines is a drug.</i>

12:29.415 --> 12:30.958
He said it!

12:31.876 --> 12:37.256
I've come directly to the police today
to reveal this truth to the public.

12:37.339 --> 12:38.466
Do you have proof?

12:38.966 --> 12:40.217
Yes.

12:41.051 --> 12:43.179
I'll explain it all now.

12:43.262 --> 12:45.639
"KINES IS A DRUG"
THE KINES REPORT

12:45.723 --> 12:47.224
Whoa. Seriously?

12:47.766 --> 12:48.767
Damn.

12:48.851 --> 12:53.647
"The... Reaper's...

12:53.731 --> 12:57.526
Blood... drop."

12:59.028 --> 13:02.114
BREATHTAKING VIEW
THE REAPER'S BLOODDROP

13:02.198 --> 13:03.699
<i>Well, that's a surprise.</i>

13:05.451 --> 13:08.329
<i>I guess Melon appreciates beauty, too.</i>

13:09.997 --> 13:11.957
<i>Where is it?</i>

13:13.584 --> 13:14.710
<i>I know this place.</i>

13:19.006 --> 13:21.592
Do you understand what you've done?

13:22.885 --> 13:23.802
Look at this.

13:24.803 --> 13:25.971
It's crashed.

13:26.055 --> 13:27.181
GOLDEN HIND HOLDINGS

13:27.264 --> 13:32.019
Azuki's family's company
is the manufacturer of Kines.

13:33.062 --> 13:36.482
This is what happens
when you act without thinking.

13:36.565 --> 13:37.566
But...

13:37.650 --> 13:38.734
That's not all.

13:39.235 --> 13:41.445
Because you've been identified,

13:41.946 --> 13:45.241
this trouble has reached
the Horns Conglomerate as well.

13:45.324 --> 13:48.369
Some are even suggesting

13:48.452 --> 13:52.623
that you offered yourself to a carnivore
in an attempt to put Kines in a bad light.

13:52.706 --> 13:56.919
Not doing anything about this
makes you an accomplice to the crime.

13:57.461 --> 13:59.338
Are you saying I should ignore this?

13:59.421 --> 14:01.382
I'm talking about your methods.

14:02.049 --> 14:05.678
Having their daughter's fiancé
expose them to the public.

14:06.178 --> 14:08.973
What do you think
Azuki's family makes of this?

14:09.056 --> 14:10.724
Did you not consider any of this?

14:12.226 --> 14:13.936
Is this about my leg?

14:14.019 --> 14:15.563
Are you trying to hide it?

14:16.188 --> 14:18.899
Are you trying to ruin your engagement?

14:20.276 --> 14:21.652
Could it be

14:22.570 --> 14:24.530
that you are not interested in women?

14:25.489 --> 14:27.825
You're really changing the subject.

14:29.785 --> 14:33.038
I'm asking you
if you are uninterested in women.

14:33.122 --> 14:35.457
Or just female deer.

14:36.667 --> 14:39.253
Regardless, this is a serious situation.

14:39.920 --> 14:42.798
I think Azuki is a wonderful woman.

14:43.924 --> 14:48.387
And yet I heard your dinner date
did not go so well.

14:48.470 --> 14:53.100
It wasn't any worse than having you
butt into our relationship like this.

14:53.183 --> 14:56.061
This is a conversation
between a president and his heir.

14:57.855 --> 14:58.939
Stand up.

15:04.445 --> 15:07.448
From the moment I bought you
for seven million,

15:07.990 --> 15:11.535
business negotiations between us
have been absolutely essential.

15:12.244 --> 15:13.829
Five hundred thousand for your antlers,

15:13.913 --> 15:16.081
and two and half million for your leg.

15:16.165 --> 15:18.250
That alone is 10 million.

15:19.209 --> 15:21.337
I don't care what detours you take.

15:21.921 --> 15:25.299
Just don't forget that you are
the heir of the Horns Conglomerate.

15:43.567 --> 15:46.278
<i>I've come near here on deliveries,</i>

15:47.404 --> 15:50.616
<i>but how long has it been
since I stared at the ocean like this?</i>

15:52.993 --> 15:58.582
<i>But a place like this...
I wish I'd come here with Haru.</i>

16:02.544 --> 16:04.838
<i>If she were here next to me,</i>

16:04.922 --> 16:08.550
<i>it'd be impossible to focus on the ocean.
I'd probably creep her out.</i>

16:09.385 --> 16:13.305
<i>I'd love to talk to her
while watching the waves.</i>

16:13.389 --> 16:17.685
<i>Though I'd be happy
just having her by my side.</i>

16:18.811 --> 16:23.774
<i>Come to think of it, I've never
been to the beach with the guys in 701.</i>

16:24.483 --> 16:26.402
<i>I'd love to swim with all of them.</i>

16:26.485 --> 16:28.570
<i>We canines love the water.</i>

16:29.196 --> 16:33.325
<i>And I'd sure love to go out to sea
with Sagwan and see his home someday.</i>

16:33.826 --> 16:35.035
<i>We could bring Seven, too.</i>

16:36.704 --> 16:38.622
<i>That sure sounds fun.</i>

16:41.375 --> 16:42.376
<i>I guess...</i>

16:43.002 --> 16:44.628
<i>I'm a pretty positive guy.</i>

16:45.546 --> 16:46.547
<i>Or maybe</i>

16:47.256 --> 16:49.091
<i>I've become more positive?</i>

16:51.301 --> 16:56.265
<i>I think I've lived a pretty fun 18 years.</i>

16:57.182 --> 16:58.350
<i>Thanks to everyone.</i>

17:00.102 --> 17:01.103
<i>But...</i>

17:01.979 --> 17:02.980
<i>For Melon...</i>

17:04.064 --> 17:07.151
<i>He might be stuck staring
at the sea alone forever.</i>

17:07.985 --> 17:09.903
<i>Waiting for someone to understand him.</i>

17:11.822 --> 17:15.534
<i>I wonder what he thinks about,
looking at the Reaper's Blooddrop.</i>

17:16.827 --> 17:19.580
<i>I wish I could talk with him one-on-one.</i>

17:21.874 --> 17:23.917
<i>Melon's leaf tattoos...</i>

17:26.086 --> 17:28.630
<i>I bet he doesn't want to show them off.</i>

17:28.714 --> 17:30.883
<i>I'm sure they're beautiful, though.</i>

17:32.426 --> 17:34.887
<i>That sloth said he was lonely.</i>

17:36.221 --> 17:37.639
<i>He said he was always alone.</i>

17:39.058 --> 17:41.310
<i>I wish he'd just talk to me.</i>

17:42.102 --> 17:43.562
<i>Maybe then he'd understa--</i>

17:53.238 --> 17:56.033
"Are you scared?"

17:58.035 --> 18:00.537
"Are you... worried?"

18:01.246 --> 18:04.249
"You must be... lonely."

18:04.833 --> 18:09.379
I am!
It's like I'm living in utter darkness!

18:11.256 --> 18:14.802
"You're... always... alone."

18:15.385 --> 18:22.226
I am!
There isn't a soul who understands me!

18:25.229 --> 18:29.108
Is that what you imagined I'd say?

18:29.191 --> 18:35.656
Thank you!
Will you be the one who understands me?

18:37.741 --> 18:42.121
However, the child born
to a leopard mother and a gazelle father

18:42.204 --> 18:45.332
is the star of a loveless tragedy.

18:45.415 --> 18:48.502
Unable to trust
the gray wolf that believed in him,

18:48.585 --> 18:52.172
he ends up killing him with his own hands.

18:52.256 --> 18:53.507
Bang.

18:53.590 --> 18:56.093
What a tragedy!

18:56.176 --> 19:00.472
You see, I have really good hearing.

19:00.556 --> 19:03.809
I knew you were following me.

19:04.977 --> 19:08.522
Though I was surprised
that you were still alive.

19:09.106 --> 19:11.233
<i>It was all a trap!</i>

19:19.158 --> 19:22.828
But hey, I'm glad we got to meet again.

19:22.911 --> 19:25.581
I'll make sure you die for good this time.

19:26.206 --> 19:29.835
So! Will you be broken by the rocks?

19:29.918 --> 19:32.421
Or will you sink into the sea and drown?

19:32.504 --> 19:33.630
Why...

19:35.215 --> 19:36.216
Why?

19:36.800 --> 19:37.926
"Why?"

19:38.719 --> 19:41.722
I just wanted to talk to you.

19:44.308 --> 19:46.768
You're too much! God, that's hilarious.

19:46.852 --> 19:50.105
"Oh... all I wanted... was to help you."

19:50.189 --> 19:52.983
Man, that's a good one!

19:53.066 --> 19:56.862
Sympathizing with me of your own accord,
putting your own expectations on me.

19:56.945 --> 20:01.283
What a wonderful world you must live in.

20:01.366 --> 20:03.202
Why are you doing this?

20:05.913 --> 20:07.748
It's just so much fun, you know?

20:07.831 --> 20:10.792
Seeing the hopeful become hopeless.

20:10.876 --> 20:13.295
It's so fun I can't help myself.

20:13.378 --> 20:15.047
Sympathy is so boring.

20:15.130 --> 20:18.300
If you want to make me happy,

20:18.383 --> 20:22.888
then die a fun, excruciating death!

20:25.641 --> 20:26.808
You're scared.

20:27.643 --> 20:30.729
Want to know what I really like?

20:32.397 --> 20:35.442
A face filled with the fear of death.

20:36.068 --> 20:40.656
No matter the species,
everyone makes the same face.

20:41.198 --> 20:44.868
An honest expression, free of lies.

20:45.577 --> 20:46.745
Melon.

20:48.622 --> 20:52.417
There it is. There's that face!

21:11.395 --> 21:13.897
The Reaper's Blooddrop, eh...

21:21.280 --> 21:23.031
Well, then.

21:36.795 --> 21:40.882
The concept of "meat" as we understand it
only came about after the war.

21:42.050 --> 21:45.178
Before that, carnivores were
known as "living creatures"...

21:45.304 --> 21:48.682
He hasn't called you, right?
Why don't you just break up?

21:50.642 --> 21:52.185
Maybe you're right.

21:52.269 --> 21:55.022
You can totally find someone better!

21:55.105 --> 21:56.106
You two.

21:57.274 --> 21:58.692
Quiet down.

21:58.775 --> 21:59.776
Sorry.

22:00.736 --> 22:04.823
So, from there, the relationship
between the two began to break down.

22:04.906 --> 22:07.868
Complicated feelings began to emerge.

22:07.951 --> 22:10.912
A love-hate relationship, if you will.

23:36.915 --> 23:41.920
Subtitle translation by: Thomas Grathwol
